<article class="env-lemma" id="0567">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0567">Lemma <span data-tag="0567">10.157.5</span>.</a> A regular ring is normal. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $R$ be a regular ring. By Lemma <a href="/tag/031S" data-tag="031S">10.157.4</a> it suffices to prove that $R$ is $(R_1)$ and $(S_2)$. As a regular local ring is Cohen-Macaulay, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00NQ" data-tag="00NQ">10.106.3</a>, it is clear that $R$ is $(S_2)$. Property $(R_1)$ is immediate. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>